# ---- Scotland: "Is your licence renewal due?" checker (free tool, no prices) ----
RCHK='24 Oct 2026'
RS={'act':('Civic Government (Scotland) Act 1982, Schedule 1, paras 2, 8(2), 8(5) and 8(5A)','https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/1982/45/schedule/1'),
'ord':('Licensing of Short-term Lets Order 2022 (SSI 2022/32), Schedule 2 para 10 (longer renewal periods)','https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ssi/2022/32/schedule/2'),
'gs1':('Scottish Government: Short-term lets licensing, Part 1 guidance for hosts and operators, section 6 (renewals)','https://www.gov.scot/publications/short-term-lets-licensing-scheme-part-1-guidance-hosts-operators/pages/6/'),
'gs2':('Scottish Government: Short-term lets licensing, Part 2 supplementary guidance, section 2 (licence duration)','https://www.gov.scot/publications/short-term-lets-licensing-scheme-part-2-supplementary-guidance-licensing-authorities-letting-agencies-booking-platforms/pages/2/')}
# Council-specific renewal facts, each checked on RCHK against the council's own pages.
RX={'highland':dict(y=3,lead=0,note='Highland Council: a full licence is normally granted for 3 years from the date of issue, and checking the expiry date is your responsibility. Renew online by choosing "Renewal of full licence". If you submit before expiry, your existing licence stays in effect and you can keep operating; the council says you do not need to apply months in advance. If you do not apply before expiry, it is unlawful to accept guests or bookings after the expiry date.',src=[('Highland Council: Renewing a short-term let licence','https://www.highland.gov.uk/short-term-lets/apply-short-term-let-licence/9'),('Highland Council: Short-term lets policy statement, section 8','https://www.highland.gov.uk/downloads/file/224/short-term-lets-policy-statement')]),
'city-of-edinburgh':dict(y=3,ysec=1,lead=0,note='City of Edinburgh Council policy: a new secondary letting licence lasts 1 year, and a secondary letting renewal lasts 1 or 3 years (normally 1 year if safety certificates were not kept up to date for the whole previous licence). Home letting and home sharing licences last 3 years. A renewal made before expiry keeps your licence in effect until the council decides, and the renewal process is the same as a new application.',src=[('City of Edinburgh Council: Short-term lets licensing policy (19 May 2025), paras 4.1, 4.2, 4.45 to 4.48','https://www.edinburgh.gov.uk/downloads/file/32060/short-term-lets-policy'),('City of Edinburgh Council: Short-term lets licensing','https://www.edinburgh.gov.uk/licences-permits/licences-permits-applications/10')]),
'argyll-and-bute':dict(y=3,lead=2,note='Argyll and Bute Council: licences are normally valid for 3 years. The council recommends you submit your renewal 2 months before your licence expires; your existing licence continues until the renewal is decided, and it is your responsibility to renew before the expiry date.',src=[('Argyll and Bute Council: Short term lets licence','https://www.argyll-bute.gov.uk/licences/short-term-lets-licence')]),
'na-h-eileanan-siar':dict(y=3,lead=3,note='Comhairle nan Eilean Siar: submit your renewal, with all documents and the fee, before your licence expires, and it must be competent (complete and verified) before the expiry date. The Comhairle recommends submitting 3 months before expiry. If a competent renewal is not in before expiry, you are treated as a new operator and cannot take bookings or guests until licensed.',src=[('Comhairle nan Eilean Siar: Short-term lets','https://www.cne-siar.gov.uk/stl')]),
'angus':dict(y=3,lead=0,note='Angus Council: a new licence lasts up to 3 years and a renewal up to 6 years. Use the expiry date printed on your licence.',src=[('Angus Council: Short-term lets, licence duration','https://www.angus.gov.uk/licences_and_permits/short_term_lets?page_id=1844')])}
RD={'chk':RCHK,'c':[]}
for c in sorted(d['councils'],key=lambda c:c['name']):
    s=slug(c)
    if c['nation']=='Scotland' and c['verified'] and s in CX:
        x=RX.get(s,{});RD['c'].append({'s':s,'n':c['name'],'y':x.get('y',3),'ysec':x.get('ysec',x.get('y',3)),'lead':x.get('lead',0),'note':x.get('note',''),'src':x.get('src',[])})
RJ=json.dumps(RD,ensure_ascii=False).replace('</','<\\/')
_rs=lambda L:'<ul class="small">'+''.join(f'<li><a href="{u}" rel="nofollow">{e(t)}</a> (checked {RCHK})</li>' for t,u in L)+'</ul>'
RCSS='<style>.rnw{display:grid;gap:.4rem;max-width:30rem}.rnw select,.rnw input{padding:.6rem;font-size:1rem;width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}.rnw label{font-weight:600;margin-top:.3rem}.rn-out .big{font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:700;margin:.3rem 0}.rn-out dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:.3rem .8rem;margin:.6rem 0}.rn-out dt{font-weight:600}.rn-out dd{margin:0}.rn-warn{background:#fff4e5;border-left:4px solid #f2a541;padding:.6rem .8rem;border-radius:6px}.nla{background:#eef5fb;border-left:4px solid #155a8a;padding:.6rem .8rem;border-radius:6px;font-weight:600}</style>'
RF='''<form class="rnw" onsubmit="return false"><label for="rn-c">Your council</label><select id="rn-c"><option value="">Choose a council</option></select><label for="rn-t">Type of let</label><select id="rn-t"><option value="sec">Secondary letting (a property you do not live in)</option><option value="home">Home letting or home sharing</option></select><label for="rn-d">Start date of your current licence (the date it was granted or came into force)</label><input type="date" id="rn-d"><label for="rn-y">Licence length (check your licence)</label><select id="rn-y"><option value="1">1 year</option><option value="2">2 years</option><option value="3" selected>3 years</option><option value="6">6 years</option></select></form><div id="rn-out" class="rn-out" aria-live="polite"></div>'''
RJS='''<script>(function(){var D=%s,C=document.getElementById('rn-c'),T=document.getElementById('rn-t'),Dt=document.getElementById('rn-d'),Y=document.getElementById('rn-y'),O=document.getElementById('rn-out'),M=['Jan','Feb','Mar','Apr','May','Jun','Jul','Aug','Sep','Oct','Nov','Dec'];
D.c.forEach(function(c){var o=document.createElement('option');o.value=c.s;o.textContent=c.n;C.appendChild(o);});var o=document.createElement('option');o.value='other';o.textContent='Another Scottish council';C.appendChild(o);
function cur(){return D.c.filter(function(c){return c.s===C.value})[0]||null}
function addM(d,m){var y=d.getUTCFullYear(),mo=d.getUTCMonth()+m,day=d.getUTCDate();var r=new Date(Date.UTC(y,mo,1));var last=new Date(Date.UTC(r.getUTCFullYear(),r.getUTCMonth()+1,0)).getUTCDate();r.setUTCDate(Math.min(day,last));return r}
function f(d){return d.getUTCDate()+' '+M[d.getUTCMonth()]+' '+d.getUTCFullYear()}
function el(t,x,cl){var e=document.createElement(t);if(x)e.textContent=x;if(cl)e.className=cl;return e}
function setLen(){var c=cur();if(!c)return;Y.value=String(T.value==='sec'?c.ysec:c.y)}
function run(){O.innerHTML='';if(!Dt.value)return;var p=Dt.value.split('-');var s=new Date(Date.UTC(+p[0],+p[1]-1,+p[2]));if(isNaN(s))return;var c=cur(),yrs=+Y.value,ex=addM(s,12*yrs),now=new Date(),td=new Date(Date.UTC(now.getFullYear(),now.getMonth(),now.getDate()));
var gather=addM(ex,-3),sub=c&&c.lead?addM(ex,-c.lead):null,days=Math.round((ex-td)/864e5);
O.appendChild(el('h3','Your estimated dates'));
O.appendChild(el('p','Estimated expiry: around '+f(ex),'big'));
var dl=el('dl');function row(a,b){dl.appendChild(el('dt',a));dl.appendChild(el('dd',b))}
row('Start gathering documents',f(gather)+' (our suggestion: about 3 months ahead, so certificates and plans are current. Not a council rule.)');
if(sub)row('Council-recommended submission',f(sub)+' ('+c.lead+' months before expiry, as recommended by '+c.n+')');
row('Latest date to apply','Before '+f(ex)+'. A renewal made before expiry keeps your licence in effect until the council decides.');
O.appendChild(dl);
if(days<0){O.appendChild(el('p','This estimated expiry date has passed. If you did not apply to renew before it, the licence has lapsed: the Scottish Government says a later application is treated as a new application, and you cannot take bookings or guests until you hold a licence. The 1982 Act lets a council, if you show good cause, treat a renewal made up to 28 days late as made on time, but that is the council\\'s choice. Do not rely on it; contact your council now.','rn-warn'))}
else if(days<=92){O.appendChild(el('p','Your licence expires in about '+days+' days. Start your renewal now.','rn-warn'))}
else{O.appendChild(el('p','About '+days+' days to go.'))}
O.appendChild(el('p','This is only an estimate. Your licence shows its expiry date, and that date (and your council\\'s own requirements) always win.','small'));
if(c){if(c.note){O.appendChild(el('h4','What '+c.n+' says'));O.appendChild(el('p',c.note));var u=el('ul','', 'small');c.src.forEach(function(x){var li=el('li'),a=el('a',x[0]);a.href=x[1];a.rel='nofollow';li.appendChild(a);li.appendChild(document.createTextNode(' (checked '+D.chk+')'));u.appendChild(li)});O.appendChild(u)}
var m=el('p'),a=el('a','See our '+c.n+' page: fees, planning and levy, with official sources');a.href='councils/'+c.s+'.html';m.appendChild(a);O.appendChild(m)}
else if(C.value==='other'){var m2=el('p'),a2=el('a','Find your council page');a2.href='councils.html';m2.appendChild(document.createTextNode('Most Scottish licences last 3 years, but councils can grant shorter ones, and longer renewals are possible. '));m2.appendChild(a2);O.appendChild(m2)}}
C.addEventListener('change',function(){setLen();run()});T.addEventListener('change',function(){setLen();run()});[Dt,Y].forEach(function(x){x.addEventListener('change',run);x.addEventListener('input',run)});})();</script>'''
_rwf=FORM.replace('<form class="signup"','<form class="signup" id="rn-wl" aria-label="Join the renewal kit waitlist"',1).replace('>Subscribe<','>Join the waitlist<')
RWL=f'''<div class="alertbox" id="waitlist"><h2>Renewal kit coming soon: join the waitlist</h2><p>We are putting together a Scottish licence renewal kit: a checklist, a document tracker and templates. Join the waitlist and we will email you when it is ready. You will also get our weekly "what changed" email. Unsubscribe any time.</p>{_rwf}<script>(function(){{var f=document.getElementById('rn-wl');if(!f||!f.utm_campaign)return;var q=new URLSearchParams(location.search);f.utm_campaign.value='renewal-kit-waitlist';f.utm_source.value=(q.get('utm_source')||f.utm_source.value||'renewal-checker').slice(0,100);f.utm_medium.value=(q.get('utm_medium')||f.utm_medium.value||'site').slice(0,100);}})();</script></div>'''
_rb=f'''<p class="lead">Enter your council and your licence start date. We estimate when your Scottish short-term let licence expires, when to start your renewal, and link to your council's page.</p>
<p class="nla">Not legal advice: this is an estimate and an organising aid. Check the expiry date on your licence and check with your council.</p>
<div class="box">{RF}</div>{RJS % RJ}
<h2>How renewal works in Scotland</h2>
<ul><li><b>Licence length.</b> A full licence lasts up to 3 years, or a shorter period set by the council. On renewal, a council can grant a longer period if it has published when it will do so. The licence must state its expiry date. Sources: <a href="{RS['act'][1]}" rel="nofollow">1982 Act Sch 1 para 8(2)</a>, <a href="{RS['ord'][1]}" rel="nofollow">2022 Order Sch 2 para 10</a>, <a href="{RS['gs2'][1]}" rel="nofollow">Part 2 guidance 2.5 to 2.8</a>.</li>
<li><b>Apply before expiry.</b> If you apply to renew before your licence expires, it stays in effect until the council decides (including any appeal period). You can apply at any time before expiry. Sources: <a href="{RS['act'][1]}" rel="nofollow">1982 Act Sch 1 para 8(5)</a>, <a href="{RS['gs1'][1]}" rel="nofollow">Part 1 guidance section 6</a>.</li>
<li><b>If it lapses.</b> If your licence expires before you apply, the Scottish Government says the application is treated as a new one, and you cannot operate until licensed. A council may, if you show good cause, treat a renewal made up to 28 days late as made on time, but that is at its discretion. Sources: <a href="{RS['gs1'][1]}" rel="nofollow">Part 1 guidance section 6</a>, <a href="{RS['act'][1]}" rel="nofollow">1982 Act Sch 1 para 8(5A)</a>.</li>
<li><b>What a renewal checks.</b> That your details are still correct, that you are still a fit and proper person, and that the premises still meet the mandatory conditions. You must display a site notice for 21 days, as for a new application. Fees and additional conditions can change from last time. Sources: <a href="{RS['gs1'][1]}" rel="nofollow">Part 1 guidance section 6</a>, <a href="{RS['act'][1]}" rel="nofollow">1982 Act Sch 1 para 2</a>.</li></ul>
{RWL}
<h2>Official sources</h2>{_rs(list(RS.values())+[s for x in RX.values() for s in x['src']])}
<p class="small">Councils we cover in the checker: {len(RD["c"])}. <a href="councils.html">See all council pages</a>. Information checked {RCHK}. The UK Short-Let Rules team.</p>'''
page('scotland-licence-renewal-checker.html','Is your Scottish short-term let licence renewal due?',_rb,desc='Free checker for Scottish short-term let hosts: estimate when your licence expires and when to start your renewal, with your council\'s renewal rules and official sources.',full_title='Short-term let licence renewal checker (Scotland) | UK Short-Let Rules Tracker',head=RCSS)
